{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FLEET LESSON (marabou incident, 2026-08-13): staging ticket descriptions at bare shared paths (/tmp/desc.md) in a parallel fleet caused a cross-agent corruption — marabou's rebar edit wrote jerboa's staged plan into marabou's ticket (repaired verbatim from EDIT event 1786615750316610001; the other ticket was never written). Rule for all implementer briefs: stage scratch files under a ticket-scoped or job-scoped path (e.g. $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/<ticket>-desc.md or the worktree), NEVER a generic /tmp name. Also note the corruption staled the attestation (the PASS was earned against the corrupted text) — the repair requires a fresh review before close, which is the gate working correctly."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786622380246465001,"uuid":"7b0abf3f-6ab6-428a-b700-0c2cf01f6870"}